taxonomy.description:
Answer with JSON only, of exactly this shape:
{"items": [{"text": "what is to be done", "owner": "who, or empty", "due": "when, or empty"}]}
Use an empty array when there is nothing to list. Do not write anything outside the JSON.

prompts.body:
Reduce this telephone call to one phrase of at most twelve words — the sort of line that would go in a table beside the caller's name. No full stop, no quotation marks.

{{artifact:summary}}

{{transcript}}

Pick out what was named in this call, as JSON of exactly this shape:
{"people": [], "companies": [], "places": [], "dates": [], "amounts": [], "references": []}
Each is a list of strings, written as they were said. Leave a list empty rather than guessing.

{{transcript}}

File this call under exactly one of these categories. Answer with its code.

{{categories}}
{{transcript}}

Which of these are true of this call? Answer with their codes, or with an empty list if none of them is.

{{tags}}
{{transcript}}

Raise any of these that this call shows. For each one, quote the words it rests on and give the moment in milliseconds where they were said. Raise nothing rather than stretching a definition.

{{red_flags}}
{{transcript}}

The other person has just said:

{{reply}}

Earlier in this conversation:

{{conversation}}

Say in one line what is happening — an objection, a question you have not answered, a sign they are ready — and in one line what to say next. If there is nothing worth saying, say only "—".

The other person has just said:

{{reply}}

Earlier in this conversation:

{{conversation}}

If they asked a question, give the answer itself, in a few short lines, out of what is common knowledge on the subject. If no question was asked, say briefly what the candidate should cover in their next reply.
